\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces $F_{max}$, $F_{avg}$, $F_{min}$ versus generation on M1 at each method's best configuration (average of 10 runs). Deterministic crowding drives all three statistics to $\approx 1$: its whole population sits on the five equal-height peaks. The standard GA's $F_{avg}$ plateaus far below the peaks, and fitness sharing settles at an intermediate $F_{avg}$ because it deliberately spreads individuals across niches and the slopes between them.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convM1}{{1}{4}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces $F_{max}$, $F_{avg}$, $F_{min}$ versus generation on M4 (average of 10 runs). Crowding's $F_{min}$ climbs steadily as the population fills the tall peaks; the standard GA and sharing keep $F_{min} \approx 0$ because valley individuals persist. All three reach $F_{max} \approx 1$ within a few generations.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convM4}{{2}{4}}
